# Read by `docker compose` itself, on the machine running it, to fill in the volume path in
# docker-compose.yaml. Copy to docker/.env (gitignored). The app's own settings (credentials,
# S3_BUCKET, AWS_*) are in docker/scanner.env.
#
# An absolute path on the Docker host, required: with none set, Docker would create an empty
# root-owned directory and mount that.

# watchlist.txt, config/local.json, runs/, report/, .cache/. Back up runs/.
STATE_DIR=/path/to/spread-scanner

# Optional: spread-book's reports/ directory on the Docker host, mounted read-only so the report can mark
# the spreads you hold (from its latest.json). Leave it out if spread-book does not run on this host.
# SPREAD_BOOK_REPORTS=/path/to/spread-book/reports
